WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.370
Welcome back, SCP Explained viewers!

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:06.040
We hope you're all having a terrible day-
I'm sorry, my mistake.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.510
I meant, we hope you're all having a wonderful
day!

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:13.970
That unfortunate linguistic mixup was brought
on by a force we're still struggling to understand.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:19.070
You see, we here at SCP Explained have fallen
under the influence of a temporal anomaly

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.939
commonly referred to as "Opposite Day."

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:25.740
You might be under the impression that Opposite
Day is just something elementary school children

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.689
came up with to excuse walking backwards and
saying things they don't mean, but you would

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:32.450
be sorely mistaken.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:37.210
It is all too real, and no one is immune to
its confusing effects!

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:41.910
In the spirit of Opposite Day, which comes
for us all no matter how much we try to prepare,

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:47.460
we decided to fire up the good old Anom-O-Tron
6000 to see how this unknowable force might

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.410
impact one of the anomalies at the SCP Foundation!

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:56.700
We all know what happens in the ordinary,
non-Opposite world when someone looks at SCP-096's

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.700
face.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:02.620
It's one of the first rules they tell new
employees at the SCP Foundation: don't look

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.680
at the Shy Guy's face!

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.330
But what if the effect was reversed?

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:13.009
What if seeing SCP-096's face didn't send
the creature into an irrepressible murderous

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:19.120
rage, but rather inspired that same mindless
violence in the ordinary person that saw it?

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.799
Let's start the simulation and find out.

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:29.350
Imagine, if you can, a world in which the
SCP Foundation did not have SCP-096 in containment,

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.430
or even know of its existence.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:36.259
It's difficult to envision a creature nearly
synonymous with the Foundation itself living

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:41.580
a life outside of those reinforced concrete
and steel walls, but that is the world in

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.860
which our story begins.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:49.530
Deep in the snow-covered forests of a remote
mountain range, a long-limbed, pale, humanoid

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:53.360
creature ran through the trees with innocent
abandon.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.570
Its white skin and long, thin arms and legs
allowed it to blend in with the snow and the

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:03.899
narrow trunks of the trees, providing a natural
camouflage from any interlopers that might

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:05.520
present a threat.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:11.361
The creature lived a largely peaceful existence,
feeding on roots, berries, and, yes, some

00:02:11.361 --> 00:02:15.810
of the local wildlife, but that's just the
way things work in nature.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:21.720
There are predators and prey, none good or
evil in the way human beings conceive of things,

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.740
all just doing their best to stay alive.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:29.340
The creature that does not think of itself
as SCP-096 had known little more than the

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:34.650
life it lived in this forest, keeping itself
hidden from view whenever hikers or explorers

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.040
happened upon its domain.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.781
It couldn't be sure what would happen if it
was found, but its instincts drove the creature

00:02:41.781 --> 00:02:44.590
to avoid detection at all costs.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:50.811
But there is no way to guarantee perfect safety
in this world, and, as it so often does, one

00:02:50.811 --> 00:02:53.629
day something went wrong.

00:02:53.629 --> 00:02:57.680
Exhausted from searching for food all day
and night, the creature decided to get some

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:03.380
rest, leaning its head against a sturdy tree
trunk and closing its eyes for a little while.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:07.900
It did not fall asleep, the creature wasn't
capable of sleep the way humans might think

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:12.700
of it, but it did allow its mind to wander
and its alertness to slip.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:18.830
It let down its guard, only for a moment...but
that was one moment too many.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:23.900
That was just enough time for its keen ears
to miss the sound of approaching footsteps,

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:27.709
muffled slightly by the thick blanket of snow
covering the ground.

00:03:27.709 --> 00:03:30.950
By the time it heard one of the hikers speak,
it was too late.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:31.950
"What is that?!"

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.420
"I'm not sure...should we get a closer look?"

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:40.129
The creature opened its eyes to find two strangers,
a man and a woman clad in heavy winter coats

00:03:40.129 --> 00:03:43.330
and hiking gear, standing just a few feet
away.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:49.300
It turned reflexively toward the sound, and
the strangers' eyes fell upon its face.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:54.660
All of a sudden, their expressions changed,
from apprehension and curiosity to a twisted

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:59.500
scowl, a mix of fear, pain, and animalistic
rage.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:04.239
The hikers each let out a primal scream and
descended on the creature, attacking it with

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:06.170
whatever they had on hand.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:10.690
The woman clawed at its face with her fingernails,
and the man pulled the heavy backpack from

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:14.920
his shoulders and began to hit the creature
with it again and again.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:20.700
The creature was far bigger, and far stronger,
than these two strangers, and it fought back

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:23.090
in an attempt to defend itself.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:28.200
It swung its massive arms at the hikers, sending
them flying in opposite directions.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.690
The woman collided with a tree, her head hitting
wood with a loud crack!

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:35.979
The man flew out of sight, disappearing over
the edge of a cliff.

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:41.340
The creature hadn't intended to hurt them,
only to keep itself safe.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.919
As the Shy Guy began to feel a pang of guilt
for the first time in its life, it heard that

00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:47.910
horrible scream again.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:53.509
The woman had regained consciousness and was
resuming her attack in full force, blood dripping

00:04:53.509 --> 00:04:57.449
from her nose and ears and staining the white
snow red.

00:04:57.449 --> 00:05:01.500
If the Shy Guy was able to speak, it would
have said "Why are you doing this?

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.560
Please, stop, I don't want to hurt you!"

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:10.160
But it couldn't say a word, so instead, it
decided to try and outrun the woman instead.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.780
It turned, and began to tear through the forest
at a swift, unnatural gait, as the woman's

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.770
screams faded away into the distance.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:22.650
As the Shy Guy had suspected, she could not
keep up with its inhuman speed, especially

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:25.870
not with the injuries she had sustained during
the fight.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:27.509
But what had happened?

00:05:27.509 --> 00:05:31.669
Why had she and the man with her flown into
such a violent rage?

00:05:31.669 --> 00:05:35.670
Something about the sight of the creature's
face had set them off.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:40.979
It had avoided detection for so long, but
it had gotten sloppy, and now its home was

00:05:40.979 --> 00:05:42.840
no longer safe.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:47.889
There was no time to rest, the creature would
have to find another safe place to hide out,

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:49.090
and soon.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:53.660
The last thing it wanted was another confrontation
with a stranger who would look at its face

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:55.819
and then erupt into violence.

00:05:55.819 --> 00:06:00.120
As the creature continued to run, leaving
the thick cover of the treeline and making

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:06.300
its way down the mountain, it wondered: would
anyone who saw its face react the same way?

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:11.160
Perhaps this was just a uniquely awful case,
perhaps this wouldn't happen again.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.949
Still, it would be best to stay out of sight.

00:06:13.949 --> 00:06:15.940
Better safe than sorry.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:21.260
Of course, the creature not yet known as SCP-096
had never heard that expression, living a

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:25.270
completely solitary life void of any idioms
or classic sayings.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:30.330
But, its feelings vis a vis safety and regret
were pretty much the same.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:34.960
The creature descended the treacherous mountain,
effortlessly navigating the unforgiven rocky

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.570
surface and deadly slicks of ice.

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:42.289
By the time the creature had left its old
mountain home behind, the sun had set and

00:06:42.289 --> 00:06:44.800
night had fallen on the wintery landscape.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.639
It slowed its stride then, listening for the
sounds of approaching potential threats, but

00:06:49.639 --> 00:06:51.740
there appeared to be no one around.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:57.110
It was just the lone pale creature, the moon
peeking out from between the clouds, and the

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.610
open unknown world ahead.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:04.000
After some time walking completely alone,
the creature spotted lights up ahead.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:09.729
It didn't understand the concept of a town,
but that was indeed what it was.

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:14.330
The creature swerved away from the majority
of the lights, and stumbled upon an old wooden

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:18.330
barn, apparently abandoned and left to rot
in the elements.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:23.250
This would be as good a place as any to rest
for a little while, to shelter from the incoming

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.780
snowstorm and stay out of sight.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:30.550
So, the Shy Guy made itself a makeshift bed
of straw, and curled up there to wait out

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:31.550
the night.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:36.240
As it lay there, thinking about the day before,
it felt a sudden wave of grief for its lost

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:41.520
home, for the changes that had come into its
life unbidden and turned it all upside down.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:45.919
The creature covered its face with its massive
hands, and began to weep.

00:07:45.919 --> 00:07:50.220
The creature was startled from its tears when
morning came, and with it, the sound of someone

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:53.930
breaking down the rotting wood beams that
lined the barn walls.

00:07:53.930 --> 00:08:00.110
It stood, looking toward the sound, and saw
the woman from the mountain, pale and shivering,

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:04.190
eyes rimmed with dark circles and face caked
in dried blood.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:09.530
She still screamed that horrible scream, tearing
away at the wood even as it ripped up the

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:11.139
flesh of her hands.

00:08:11.139 --> 00:08:16.099
She was missing one boot, and her coat was
torn open, scattering tiny feathers with every

00:08:16.099 --> 00:08:17.099
movement.

00:08:17.099 --> 00:08:22.130
She did not appear to feel the cold, the pain,
the exhaustion of chasing the creature for

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:23.410
so long.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:29.460
She only wanted one thing, to destroy the
creature by any means necessary.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:34.080
With a screech like a banshee, she leapt onto
the creature's back, clawing at its face and

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.120
eyes.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:40.070
It thrashed wildly, throwing the woman to
the ground, and running without a glance back.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:44.159
Maybe she survived her fall onto the cold
hard ground, or maybe it would be the blow

00:08:44.159 --> 00:08:46.540
that actuallly finished her off.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:51.050
The creature's only priority was to keep moving
before something else tried to attack.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:55.589
What the creature didn't know was that the
citizens of the nearby town, the one that

00:08:55.589 --> 00:09:00.029
it was about to run right into the center
of in its panic, were gathering to celebrate

00:09:00.029 --> 00:09:04.630
their annual Christmas festival, complete
with an early-morning parade through the town

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:05.630
square.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:11.149
The same town square that the Shy Guy was
bounding into at that exact moment.

00:09:11.149 --> 00:09:15.959
As the Shy Guy raced over the cobblestone
street, it ran directly into the line of sight

00:09:15.959 --> 00:09:21.120
of a full marching band, a fleet of dancers
dressed in costumes inspired by The 12 Days

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:26.360
of Christmas, a row of young women competing
in the Miss Holiday Spirit pageant, and a

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:30.490
jolly old man dressed up as Santa Claus in
his sleigh.

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:34.810
The marching band saw the creature first,
terror morphing quickly into that same wordless

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:37.839
rage as their eyes fell on its face.

00:09:37.839 --> 00:09:43.180
It moved to cover itself, to hide its face
from view, but it was too late.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:47.660
The marching band swarmed around it, swinging
trombones and clarinets.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:51.830
One percussion player broke a massive bass
drum over the creature's head in the struggle.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:57.090
Still, it was able to withstand the musical
onslaught, flinging musicians this way and

00:09:57.090 --> 00:10:02.310
that, snapping brass instruments like twigs
and crushing woodwinds into mulch.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:06.840
Unfortunately, as the marching band was being
dealt with, the commotion had drawn the attention

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:09.920
of the dancers and the pageant competitors.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:15.170
One swarm was replaced with two more as the
performers flew into a frenzy, tackling the

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:19.450
creature to the ground and using every item
at their disposal to try and harm it.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:24.279
The creature bellowed with fear and frustration,
prying itself free again and continuing to

00:10:24.279 --> 00:10:25.279
run.

00:10:25.279 --> 00:10:30.290
This time, it actually remembered to cover
its face, just in time to pass Saint Nicholas

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:31.290
himself.

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.470
"Have you all gone mad?"

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:38.040
The old man had not gotten the chance to see
the creature's face himself, and was horrified

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.110
at the behavior of his friends and neighbors.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.230
"What's gotten into you?"

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:46.210
The creature was preoccupied with running
and keeping its face covered, so it did not

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:47.920
see what happened next.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:52.269
It could only hear the sound of the Santa
Claus impersonator confronting the mob, his

00:10:52.269 --> 00:10:57.410
scandalized shouts becoming suddenly muffled,
and the troubling sound of silence followed

00:10:57.410 --> 00:11:00.790
by the thundering stampede of crazed villagers.

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:05.450
The man had tried to help, but there was only
one of him, and there were so many others

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:07.870
intent on destroying the creature now.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:14.029
So, the Shy Guy continued to run for its life,
listening to the mob just behind it, never

00:11:14.029 --> 00:11:17.519
stopping to rest, to eat or sleep.

00:11:17.519 --> 00:11:21.600
Whatever had filled these people with such
murderous impulse, it made them something

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:24.410
a little removed from human too.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:28.760
They were sustained by the desire to kill,
even when their bodies should have given out

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:30.120
long ago.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:34.730
As the creature ran, it encountered more people
that caught a glimpse of its face, that lost

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:39.870
themselves in the urge to destroy, and became
one with the growing horde.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:43.970
The creature could no longer tell how long
it had been running, or if it would ever be

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.670
able to stop.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:51.300
It was strong and seemingly invulnerable,
but how long would it be until enough people

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:56.660
were caught in this curse, until the mob was
big enough to swallow the creature whole?

00:11:56.660 --> 00:12:00.100
Just when it was beginning to contemplate
giving up, lying down and letting the sea

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:04.680
of angry faces overtake it, a burlap bag was
thrown over its head.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:08.480
It skidded to a stop, disoriented, feeling
around.

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:09.630
"Quick!

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:13.130
Get it out of here!

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:14.130
We need amnestics, lots of them!

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:15.130
These people look nuts!"

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:18.320
A voice barked orders, as the creature felt
hands pushing it into a small enclosed space.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:23.699
The back of an SCP Foundation van, though
of course the Shy Guy didn't know that.

00:12:23.699 --> 00:12:26.769
It could hear more voices whispering to each
other, close by.

00:12:26.769 --> 00:12:30.639
"I've never seen anything like this...what
is this thing, anyway?"

00:12:30.639 --> 00:12:31.639
"Stop!

00:12:31.639 --> 00:12:33.350
Whatever you do, don't look at its face."

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:40.329
Now go check out “SCP-096 Origin Theories”
and “SCP-096 Tale - A Lesson In Power”

00:12:40.329 --> 00:12:41.720
for more tales of the Shy Guy!

